[5.355786, "o", "\u001b[1m{\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m\"id\"\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\"resp_47204\"\u001b[39m\u001b[1m,\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m\"status\"\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\"completed\"\u001b[39m\u001b[1m,\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m\"output\"\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\"**QUIC Overview**\\n\\nQUIC (Quick UDP Internet Connections) is a TCPv3 (Transmission Control Protocol v3) extension that provides a high-performance, low-latency, and secure way to transfer data over the internet. It was designed to replace TCP in certain scenarios, offering improved performance and re \u001b[61;1H…\"\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[1m}\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[3.003358, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m\u001b[1m↳ Watch the Praxis log pane: rehydrated history exceeded the\r\n  threshold, so the prior turns were summarized before forwarding.\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
